WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:08.260
A secure AWS Lambda baseline for .NET starts with clean deployment packages and least-privilege execution roles.

2
00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:18.360
Ship only the runtime artifacts the function needs, protect build outputs and deployment logs, and keep permissions narrow enough that reviewers can explain each action and resource.

3
00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.600
Treat every event source as a trust boundary.

4
00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:37.220
Secure HTTP exposure through the appropriate front door and authorization controls, validate events before side effects, use governed secret handling for sensitive values, and review VPC access, service boundaries, and network assumptions.

5
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:41.820
Design for retries, duplicate events, and partial failures.

6
00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:53.280
Idempotent processing, dead-letter handling, destinations, retry limits, alerting, and recovery steps should be part of the workload design rather than added after production failures.

7
00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:59.800
Finally, align concurrency, timeouts, memory, storage, and downstream capacity.

8
00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:08.620
Redact logs, monitor failure signals, and keep operational review connected to code, IAM, configuration, and deployment automation.

9
00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:13.200
Secure Lambda work is practical engineering across the full function lifecycle.
